e-security-metrics walkthrough log — 2026-10-10
Worked-case lesson: no command line by design (brief §6).
The "run" is the SOC metrics specification authored and self-reviewed in-session.

Scope: fictional Alderpoint Mutual SOC (continued).
Artifacts authored:
  - KPI set (4): critical-vuln MTTR (weekly, >30d -> program review); backup
    verification rate (monthly, <100% -> immediate investigation); training
    completion (quarterly, <95% -> manager escalation); phishing report rate
    (per campaign, rising click rate -> targeted retraining).
  - KRI set (4): aged criticals >30d (weekly, >10 -> CISO briefing); un-MFA'd
    privileged accounts (weekly, >0 -> immediate ticket); unencrypted PII
    stores (quarterly sample, any -> accept-or-remediate in 30d); mean analyst
    triage time (monthly trend review).
  - Six-field spec per measure: definition, data source, collection method,
    cadence, target->action, owner.
  - Collection design: automated except quarterly stratified discovery sample
    (method documented); gaming spot-check (analyst recomputes 2 numbers by
    hand quarterly).
  - Stated unmeasured gap: mean time to detect (SIEM migration in progress;
    unreliable until Q3 — honest, dated).

Self-review checklist (2026-10-10):
  [x] every measure serves a named decision (no vanity metrics)
  [x] KPI and KRI sections separate ("performing well but exposed" expressible)
  [x] target->action field present on every row (the load-bearing field)
  [x] collection reproducible by the next analyst (method documented)
  [x] spec-required measures present: backup verification + training completion
  [x] SP 800-55 cited as Vol. 1 + Vol. 2 (Dec 2024), NOT the withdrawn Rev. 1
      (withdrawal verified in-session: superseded 2024-12-04)
  [x] differentiated from e-security-program (measurement-program view, not
      board-memo view)
  [x] no invented statistics; company labeled fictional throughout
Nothing unrun: worked-case lessons have no CLI steps to mark.
